_info() {
    cat <<'EOF'
>>> ngscopeclient requires a working Vulkan stack

ngscopeclient renders through Vulkan (via GLFW), so it needs BOTH a Vulkan
loader and a hardware driver. The loader (vulkan-icd-loader) is pulled in
automatically, but the driver depends on your GPU and must be installed by
you:

    AMD    (Mesa RADV)   pacman -S vulkan-radeon
    Intel  (Mesa ANV)    pacman -S vulkan-intel
    NVIDIA (proprietary) pacman -S nvidia-utils
    NVIDIA (Nouveau)     pacman -S vulkan-nouveau
    VirtIO GPU (VM)      pacman -S vulkan-virtio
    No GPU / software    pacman -S vulkan-swrast   (lavapipe, slow)

Verify the stack before reporting a bug:

    pacman -S vulkan-tools
    vulkaninfo --summary        # must list a real device, not llvmpipe-only
    ls /usr/share/vulkan/icd.d/ # should contain at least one *.json
EOF
}

_troubleshooting() {
    cat <<'EOF'

>>> If startup fails with:
>>>   ERROR: glfwGetRequiredInstanceExtensions failed, code 0 ((null))

This almost always means the Vulkan loader found NO driver (ICD), so the
instance extension list lacks VK_KHR_surface. Do NOT assume the package or
your GPU driver is broken -- the usual cause is a stale override.

1) Check for overriding environment variables:

       env | grep -iE 'VK_|VULKAN'

   VK_DRIVER_FILES / VK_ICD_FILENAMES REPLACE the loader's default search
   path. If they point at files that do not exist (a common leftover from
   copying AMD tuning snippets, e.g. radeon_icd.i686.json or
   radeon_icd.x86_64.json -- Arch ships radeon_icd.json without the
   architecture suffix), the loader finds nothing at all.

2) Confirm with the loader's own diagnostics:

       VK_LOADER_DEBUG=error,warn ngscopeclient

   Lines like "Failed to open JSON file ..." name the offending path.

3) Fix: unset/remove those variables (commonly in /etc/environment,
   ~/.config/environment.d/*.conf or your shell rc). Logging out and back in
   is required for /etc/environment and environment.d changes to apply.

       # quick test without editing anything:
       env -u VK_DRIVER_FILES -u VK_ICD_FILENAMES ngscopeclient

   Letting the loader auto-discover /usr/share/vulkan/icd.d/*.json is the
   most robust configuration -- it keeps working if you later switch between
   RADV and AMDVLK.
EOF
}

post_install() {
    _info
    _troubleshooting
}

post_upgrade() {
    _info
    _troubleshooting
}
